    {
      "id": "sol.hmmt-nov-guts-2013-p12.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "\\((30,92)\\) OR \\((92,30)\\) If \\(a^{2}+b^{2}=2 c\\), then \\(\\left(\\frac{a+b}{2}\\right)^{2}+\\left(\\frac{a-b}{2}\\right)^{2}=\\frac{2 a^{2}+2 b^{2}}{4}=\\frac{a^{2}+b^{2}}{2}=c\\). Thus, \\(n=\\frac{62+122}{2}=92\\) and \\(m=\\frac{122-62}{2}=30\\) works.",
